WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.992
Strategy A and strategy B both grow

2
00:00:02.992 --> 00:00:04.896
8% a year.

3
00:00:05.196 --> 00:00:09.023
Halfway through, the two rides look very different.

4
00:00:09.323 --> 00:00:10.862
Both end at $216.

5
00:00:10.862 --> 00:00:14.688
B swings twice as far to get there.

6
00:00:14.988 --> 00:00:17.681
The Sharpe ratio is return divided by

7
00:00:17.681 --> 00:00:19.969
volatility: return per bump.

8
00:00:20.269 --> 00:00:22.577
A: 8 over 8 is 1.0.

9
00:00:22.577 --> 00:00:25.635
B: 8 over 16 is 0.5.

10
00:00:25.935 --> 00:00:27.858
Same gain, half the ride.

11
00:00:27.858 --> 00:00:33.085
That is what a higher Sharpe ratio means.
